-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': 'Change made in 
`src/components/TaskList.tsx` (only file touched):\n- Added a local `query` 
state and a `type="search"` input with `aria-label="Search tasks"` above the 
list.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over task titles 
(`toLowerCase().includes`), computed as `visibleTasks`; selection state remains 
in `App`, so hiding a row never clears the selected task and the detail card is 
unaffected.\n- A non-empty query renders a `Clear search` button. Clearing 
resets the query, restores all tasks, and the button stays mounted while it 
holds focus (tracked via `keepClearVisible`, released on blur or on the next 
input change), so focus remains on that button after clearing.\n- When nothing 
matches, the list is replaced by exactly `No tasks match your search.`; the 
existing `ul.task-list` markup, selected-row class, select and edit handlers are
unchanged.\n\nExact command run (via `verify_frontend`):\n- `npm run 
verify:agent` → `npm run build && npm run test:public` (tsc, vite build, 6 
Playwright tests) — exit 0, all 6 passed.\n\nRemaining risks:\n- No new 
automated coverage for the search interaction was added (existing public tests 
untouched); behavior was validated only by build/type-check and the existing 
suite.\n- The `Clear search` button intentionally persists briefly after 
clearing (until blur) to satisfy the focus requirement; a future check expecting
it to disappear instantly on an empty query would need re-review.\n- New classes
(`task-search`, `task-search-input`, `task-list-panel`, `task-empty`) have no 
dedicated CSS yet, so the control uses default input/button styling.', 'aid': 
